# GitHub Packages hosts a full npm registry, and scoped packages of this org
# resolve there (publishing targets it too — see publishConfig in package.json).
#
# No credential lives in this file, on purpose. pnpm refuses to expand
# environment variables in auth settings that come from a *project* .npmrc,
# precisely because that file is committed and could leak a token to an
# attacker-controlled registry — so a `_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` line here
# would be silently ignored, not merely redundant.
#
# Put the token where pnpm still expands it:
#   - locally, in your user-level ~/.npmrc
#     //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=YOUR_TOKEN
#   - in CI, actions/setup-node writes exactly that file for you and points
#     NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG at it, fed from NODE_AUTH_TOKEN.
@agrica:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
